<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/medical">Medical</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">Hearing Aid Assembly</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Medical products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s active" href="/markets/medical/hearing-aid-assembly"><span class="abbr">HA</span><span class="label">Hearing Aid Assembly</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/mems-sensors"><span class="abbr">MS</span><span class="label">Medical MEMS &amp; Sensors</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/pcba"><span class="abbr">PB</span><span class="label">Medical PCBA</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/medical/wireless-charging"><span class="abbr">WC</span><span class="label">Wireless Charging</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the device does and the regulatory route it follows and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Medical &middot; Hearing Aid Assembly</div><h1 class="mk-h1">Hearing aid assembly</h1><p class="mk-lede">A hearing aid is one of the smallest complete electronic products built in volume, and the assembly problem is volumetric before it is anything else: every component, interconnect and acoustic part has to be placed and attached inside an enclosure with no spare space to work in. Hana builds these devices on dedicated medical lines — micro-miniature placement and attach, acoustic component integration, and unit-level traceability carried through the build rather than reconstructed afterwards.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-hearing-aid-assembly" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ Hearing Aid Assembly &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-hearing-aid-assembly" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hearing-aid and Bluetooth test rigs are in-house, so acoustic and wireless verification runs on our own floor. The same lines assemble AI hearing aids and the wireless charging cases built alongside them. Micro-assembly is a long-standing Hana discipline; here it runs inside a medical quality system.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Complete hearing devices</span></div><div class="desc">micro-miniature assembly of hearing aids, including AI hearing aids, built and tested as finished units on dedicated medical lines.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Acoustic component integration</span></div><div class="desc">microphone and receiver integration handled as part of the micro-assembly, not as a separate downstream step.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Wireless charging cases</span></div><div class="desc">the charging case assembled alongside the device itself, with coil winding and assembly in the same company. See Wireless charging for medical devices.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Test and traceability coverage</span></div><div class="desc">hearing-aid and Bluetooth test rigs in-house, with material, unit and product traceability recorded through the build and functional test available to the program's requirements.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Process depth sits on the capability page: Micro Assembly owns the placement and interconnect processes that miniature-scale build rests on, and the accuracies they hold.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/microelectronic-assembly/micro-assembly">Explore Micro Assembly <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Assembly at hearing-device scale</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">The difficulty in a hearing device is that miniaturization and medical control have to hold at the same time. Placement and attach happen at a scale where handling itself is a process risk, so the work runs on dedicated medical lines under controlled handling rather than on general assembly. Acoustic components are integrated in-line and verified on hearing-aid test rigs rather than assumed good. Bluetooth and wireless functions can be tested on the same floor. Each unit is tied to its materials and its build record, so an individual device can be traced back through the line — which is what a regulated program, and any subsequent change to it, depends on.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">micro-miniature assembly, dedicated medical lines</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">hearing-device assembly, dedicated medical SMT</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What hearing-device work can Hana perform?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Complete hearing-aid assembly, including AI hearing aids, from micro-miniature placement and acoustic component integration through to a tested finished unit — plus the wireless charging cases built alongside them.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How small can Hana assemble?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Hearing aids and MEMS sensors are among the smallest assemblies we build, and micro-miniature work is a core part of Hana's microelectronics discipline. The exact envelope for a given device is confirmed with our team against your design.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What quality system covers hearing-aid production?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Hearing-device work runs on dedicated medical lines under an ISO 13485 quality system, with documentation, change control and material, unit and product traceability built into the process.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/medical" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Medical market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your hearing-device program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>
